Assessment: Module 15a Quiz + Final Exam + Year-end Portfolio

===============================================================================
COURSE SUMMARY
===============================================================================

SEMESTER BREAKDOWN:
• Semester 1 (Fall): Weeks 1-16, Modules 1-6, 48 hours (24 lab + 24 theory)
• Semester 2 (Spring): Weeks 17-32, Modules 7-15a, 48 hours (24 lab + 24 theory)
• TOTAL: 32 weeks, 16 modules, 96 hours (48 lab + 48 theory)

KEY TEACHING STRATEGIES:

Session Structure (1.5 hours each):
• Opening (10 min): Review, warm-up, or preview
• Main Content (60-70 min): Core instruction or lab work
• Synthesis (10-20 min): Summary, connections, next steps

Session A Focus (Theory Sessions):
• Interactive lectures with demonstrations
• Problem-solving workshops
• Concept mapping and discussion
• Mathematical applications

Session B Focus (Lab Sessions):
• Hands-on experiments and investigations
• Data collection and analysis
• Technology integration
• Collaborative problem-solving

Assessment Philosophy:
• Formative: Daily check-ins, lab observations, peer discussions
• Summative: Module quizzes, lab reports, projects, exams
• Authentic: Real-world applications, research projects, presentations

Time Management Benefits:
• Deep Learning: 1.5 hours allows for complex investigations
• Lab Completion: Full experiments can be completed in single sessions
• Discussion Time: Extended time for synthesis and reflection
• Individual Support: Time for differentiated instruction

This complete plan maximizes the 3-hour weekly format to provide deep, hands-on learning experiences while covering all 16 modules comprehensively across the full academic year.
